WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.150
- I hear we have this in common.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.550
You are a homebody, you
like to be in bed by nine.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.072
- Yes, I actually did not--

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.990
- That's me!

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.510
- All the work stuff
that happens after that,

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.101
I'm like, you're not gonna get much.

00:00:10.101 --> 00:00:10.934
(audience laughing)

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:11.767
- [Kelly] You're not gonna get anything.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:14.158
- I get glassy-eyed and I
just wanna have my snacks.

00:00:14.158 --> 00:00:16.250
Tuck my shirt into my PJs.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.780
- In my PJs, call it a night.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.058
- Yep, call it a night,
get in bed, and do this.

00:00:20.058 --> 00:00:21.136
(audience laughing)

00:00:21.136 --> 00:00:22.210
- Now I love that, I love that.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.330
And here's the thing I love about you,

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.650
you're so normal.
(audience laughing)

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.170
When we were at the
AMAs, you were hosting.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.980
And I was like, "Oh my god, I love her."

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.547
I'm sitting here going off,
and all of a sudden I'm like,

00:00:31.547 --> 00:00:34.284
"Why is Diana Ross getting
onstage with all her family?"

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:35.117
(laughing)

00:00:35.117 --> 00:00:36.640
I was like, I had no idea.
- I love that.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.970
- This 2017
(audience laughing)

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.940
like that this happened.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.020
And I'm like a fan of
you and I had no idea.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.840
- [Tracee] I love that,
at least my career worked.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.754
- No, you're so good, you're so talented.

00:00:46.754 --> 00:00:47.587
- Thank you.

00:00:47.587 --> 00:00:48.850
- I had no idea and then
it kinda made sense,

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.590
the talent doesn't fall far from the tree,

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.120
but I was like, wow.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.540
Then I was like, "You're so normal."

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.373
I would have never guessed

00:00:54.373 --> 00:00:55.490
that you would have grown up in Hollywood.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.544
I would have guessed you grew up--

00:00:56.544 --> 00:00:57.504
- Well I didn't grow up in Hollywood,

00:00:57.504 --> 00:00:59.034
I grew up in my mom's house.

00:00:59.034 --> 00:01:00.650
(audience laughing)
- Well, okay, okay.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:01.710
- And we weren't in Hollywood.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.720
We didn't live here,
only when I was little.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:04.553
- You didn't like go out or anything.

00:01:04.553 --> 00:01:07.410
- No, and I mean, my mom is such a mom.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.310
She's a mom before she's anything else.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.070
And so I just had a really--

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:11.903
- [Kelly] That's why you're great!

00:01:11.903 --> 00:01:13.130
- Yeah, I had like a
really regular upbringing.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.560
I got a lot of siblings.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:15.393
You know what I mean?

00:01:15.393 --> 00:01:17.277
My mom was always like,
"This money is not for you.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.480
"This money is for me."

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:19.860
- That's me!
- Know what I mean?

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.450
- My kids are like, "We have money."

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.517
I'm like, "No, sir,

00:01:22.517 --> 00:01:24.457
- [Both] "I have money."
(laughing)

00:01:24.457 --> 00:01:25.779
- You're broke.

00:01:25.779 --> 00:01:26.730
You ain't got any money.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:27.870
- You didn't do a thing.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.178
- I'm spending all of
this, you better get a job.

00:01:30.178 --> 00:01:32.177
- That's exactly what
she used to say to us.

00:01:32.177 --> 00:01:34.050
She was like, "I don't
know, you better figure out

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:34.883
"what you're doing."
- I just bought a ranch,

00:01:34.883 --> 00:01:35.716
I hope y'all figure it out.

00:01:35.716 --> 00:01:37.507
- She's like, "I'll pay
for doctors and make sure

00:01:37.507 --> 00:01:40.007
"there's a roof over your
head until a certain point.

00:01:40.007 --> 00:01:40.840
"And then go on."

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.800
- I'll pay for health and
education, nothing else.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:43.840
- Yeah, that's it.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.300
- 'Cause you know and
I turned out just fine

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.133
and I didn't have anything.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.650
I worked hard, so.
(audience cheering)

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.240
I find that amazing, though.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.720
'Cause my big fear as a
parent of having kids,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.553
now we have four kids,

00:01:53.553 --> 00:01:55.720
my husband and I grew up
very humble beginnings

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.257
and we're always like,
"How do parents do it

00:01:58.257 --> 00:02:01.077
"where your kids don't turn out in rehab

00:02:01.077 --> 00:02:02.269
"or like something crazy."

00:02:02.269 --> 00:02:04.350
- I think it's the value of relationship,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.560
the value of family and
the value of working.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.190
I mean, my mom is hard worker

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:13.190
and I learned all of that from
her by example, not just--

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.640
- Pressure, okay, interesting.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.370
- Yeah, you gotta be a good person, Kelly!

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.670
- I'm trying, Tracee!
(laughing)

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.720
Apparently though I'm not
as good as Quee over there.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.450
Promise's mom is gonna write
a book and help us all out.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.680
Quee's killing me in the
parent department, it's fine.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.740
But you, big news though.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.160
You actually posted the Girlfriends,

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.168
you're having a reunion, right?

00:02:31.168 --> 00:02:34.343
(audience cheering)
I'm excited, I'm excited!

00:02:34.343 --> 00:02:37.870
- You know, "Girlfriends"
ran for eight seasons,

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.860
173 episodes, we were
important to so many people,

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:45.510
and it's been 11 years
that we've been off the air

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.640
and surreal experience
bringing the Girlfriends

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.840
on to "Black-ish", it was
like a merging of worlds.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.663
So, yeah, they are coming on
this season as my girlfriends.

00:02:56.861 --> 00:02:57.790
- [Kelly] I love it!

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.085
- It was like no time had passed.

00:03:00.085 --> 00:03:01.762
I mean the love, the giggles,

00:03:01.762 --> 00:03:02.595
- [Kelly] Those are the good friends.

00:03:02.595 --> 00:03:04.820
- [Tracee] The chemistry
was like right back,

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:05.653
just right back.

00:03:05.653 --> 00:03:06.486
It was amazing.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.730
- Do you, in your personal life,
have those kinda girls too?

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.500
- Absolutely, you can't live without them.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.690
- [Kelly] No.
- Oh my god.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:12.620
- My husband can't stand it,

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.283
but I have so many female friends.

00:03:14.283 --> 00:03:16.770
- But I feel like a
lot of my best friends,

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.510
their husbands know that
their marriage doesn't work

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.700
if it's not for the friends.
(laughing)

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:23.783
- You can go, we're still gonna be here.

00:03:23.783 --> 00:03:26.614
- But it's like the balance,
you know what I mean?

00:03:26.614 --> 00:03:30.004
Like you want me, you want
me to help balance this out.

00:03:30.004 --> 00:03:32.340
- You need me.
- You need me, okay.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.470
- And you're welcome.
- Exactly. (laughing)

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.690
- I talked her off the ledge.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.320
- Yeah, I have a really good tribe

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.850
of incredible girlfriends.

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.500
- I think you need that,
like men and women,

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.860
you just need that kind of close circle

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.200
that you can really just bare all

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.670
and be gross in front of

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.310
and mean if you wanna just vent, you know?

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.780
- And that can see you when
you can't see yourself,

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.220
that can ground you.
- Call you out.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.670
- You know, I feel like
one of my best friends

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.319
really anchors me to
the best part of myself.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:00.970
And really my friends are people

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.010
that I run things by when I'm scared.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.180
And I have to say, that's
the beauty of text messages,

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.490
'cause you can be in a
room full of people having

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:10.610
really awful feelings inside,
that soup of emotions,

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.730
and you can text your best
friends and get that shot

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.460
of God, of love, of support,

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.293
- [Kelly] Humor.

00:04:17.293 --> 00:04:19.210
- Of humor without anybody knowing.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.840
And so yeah, my friends are, they're key.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.040
- That's awesome!

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.330
So you're executive
producing, is it a spinoff?

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.198
- I just love the way
that sounds, I'm so sorry.

00:04:27.198 --> 00:04:28.981
(laughing)

00:04:28.981 --> 00:04:30.548
- You're an executive producer.

00:04:30.548 --> 00:04:32.113
(audience cheering)

00:04:32.113 --> 00:04:34.380
And it is, it's awesome.
- It sounds amazing.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.803
- Here's my thing
though, with "Mixed-Ish",

00:04:35.803 --> 00:04:37.660
it's a spinoff, it's
your character, right?

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.330
- It is a spinoff, it's
my character, a flashback.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.759
So I am not physically--
- [Kelly] Oh like a prequel.

00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:43.150
- Yes, it's a prequel.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:45.230
I am not physically, that sounds
like perfume or something,

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:46.063
I don't know that sounds like--

00:04:46.063 --> 00:04:47.330
- Let's come out with it, prequel.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.200
- Okay, yeah, prequel.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.050
So it is a flashback, I'm
not physically on the show,

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.030
it is my voice, so it's my voiceover

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:54.283
kind of like "Wonder Years",
remember "Wonder Years"?

00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:55.880
- Oh so it's you as a kid, yeah?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:56.713
- Yes, it's me as a kid.

00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:58.181
- Of course I remember "Wonder Years".

00:04:58.181 --> 00:04:59.860
- The lovely young girl that is playing me

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.981
looks more like me than me.

00:05:00.981 --> 00:05:03.040
(laughing)

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:03.873
- I love that.

00:05:03.873 --> 00:05:04.750
- Like it's really weird.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.850
I'm like, "Oh my god, you're
me, but you're not me.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.119
"Like I don't understand."

00:05:08.119 --> 00:05:09.390
It's so weird.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:13.670
But she's so great and yes,
it's fish out of water comedy

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:16.570
and it's that story of what
all of us are dealing with

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.780
when we're not like
everybody else in the room

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.730
and how do you find out who you are

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:22.800
and hold on to that.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.800
- Absolutely, 100%.
(audience clapping)

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.100
That's beautiful.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.280
Well you have a new hair
line as well, right?

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.320
Yes you do!

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.430
This is my favorite thing though,

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.270
you've been working on this hair line

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:34.560
for what, 20 years? (laughs)

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.620
- 20 years of dreaming,
10 years of working on it.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.010
I wrote my first haircare
brand pitch in 2008

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:39.970
when "Girlfriends" finished

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.790
and it's taken me 10
years to make it happen.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:42.623
- Oh my gosh.
(audience cheering)

00:05:42.623 --> 00:05:45.610
- It is for--
- It's a labor of love.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.740
- It is for Promise, it is for me,

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.900
it is for curly, coily,
and tight-textured hair.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.340
It is a community of people
that have not been supported

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:58.550
and celebrated in our
beauty and our glory--

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.383
- And represented.

00:05:59.383 --> 00:06:03.320
- Yes, and we all know
that key is products.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.710
You gotta get products that work,

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.060
that hydrate and nourish your hair,

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:08.490
make it healthy and juicy and joyful,

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.515
and that's what Pattern,
my haircare products, do.

00:06:11.515 --> 00:06:13.576
(audience cheering)

00:06:13.576 --> 00:06:15.766
- I love it, I love it!

00:06:15.766 --> 00:06:18.740
You're literally one of
my favorite people ever.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.080
We've talked hair, we've talked career,

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.070
we've talked family, body.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.130
You have alter egos, though.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:24.963
- Make it bigger, hold on.

00:06:24.963 --> 00:06:25.800
- [Kelly] And I've seen these.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:26.856
Get it really big.

00:06:26.856 --> 00:06:28.207
- Yes!
- Yas!

00:06:28.207 --> 00:06:30.890
No, but you have these
alter egos that you do.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.700
And I've only, are there
three, 'cause I've seen three.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.536
- There's actually five,
but you know of three.

00:06:34.536 --> 00:06:35.369
- Okay, I've only seen three.

00:06:35.369 --> 00:06:36.513
What's the one with the
lips up to here and the--

00:06:36.513 --> 00:06:39.540
- Oh, Madame Hiver,
you're dear, sweetheart.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.820
- Oh my god, I love you!

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:43.536
- Yeah, she's a bit of an
alcoholic, there she is.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:44.420
- [Kelly] That's my favorite!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.496
- Yeah, she's a dear.

00:06:45.496 --> 00:06:48.090
(laughing)
You're a dear.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.278
She likes to drink brown alcohol.

00:06:50.278 --> 00:06:51.420
- Oh my god, I love it.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.340
Wait, you also have the rapper, right?

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.396
- T-Murda.
- [Kelly] Yeah, T-Murda.

00:06:55.396 --> 00:06:56.763
Look at her, Quee knows!

00:06:56.763 --> 00:06:59.350
- Yeah, T-Murda and then
there's Caliope Champignon

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.170
who's a fashion stylist, architect.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.780
And she never speak French,
but she speak English

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:05.613
with a French accent and this is...

00:07:05.613 --> 00:07:07.560
- Oh my god, that is so sexy.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.381
I didn't even hear anything,
all I heard was dialect,

00:07:09.381 --> 00:07:10.697
it was so pretty, it was so good.

00:07:10.697 --> 00:07:11.530
(laughing)

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.155
- Yeah, so yes, oui.

00:07:13.155 --> 00:07:14.060
- Wow, that's so Meryl Streep!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.480
You just went Meryl Streep on me!

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:17.916
You just like brought
out all these accents!

00:07:17.916 --> 00:07:20.505
(audience cheering)
Like I'm like what?

00:07:20.505 --> 00:07:21.517
That was so hot!

